<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Black Soil</title>

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/backend.css">
</head>

<body>

<div class="page">
    <%- include("partials/header") %>

    <div class="main">
        <%- include("partials/sidebar") %>

        <section class="blackbox">

            <h1>🪴 Black Soil (Regur Soil)</h1> <br>

            <img src="https://tse1.mm.bing.net/th/id/OIP.N1k02N1kNM9ihSSc6I3mwAHaE7?pid=Api&P=0&h=180" alt="Black soil"> <br>

            <b>📍 Found in India’s Deccan Plateau:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Maharashtra</li>
                <li>Madhya Pradesh</li>
                <li>Gujarat</li>
                <li>Telangana</li>
                <li>Andhra Pradesh</li>
                <li>Karnataka</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>🔬 Characteristics of Black Soil</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Color: Black to dark brown</li>
                <li>Texture: Clayey and deep</li>
                <li>High moisture-holding capacity</li>
                <li>Cracks in summer (self-ploughing)</li>
                <li><b>Rich in:</b> Calcium, Magnesium, Iron, Potash</li>
                <li><b>Poor in:</b> Nitrogen, Phosphorus</li>
                <li>Slightly alkaline</li>
            </ul>

            <hr>

            <h2>🌾 Crops Suitable for Black Soil</h2>

            <b>1️⃣ Cotton (Best crop)</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Season: Kharif</li>
                <li>Rainfall: 50–100 cm</li>
                <li>Temperature: 21–30°C</li>
                <li>Duration: 160–200 days</li>
                <li>Reason: Retains moisture well</li>
            </ul>

            <b>2️⃣ Sugarcane</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Rainfall: 75–150 cm</li>
                <li>Temperature: 20–35°C</li>
                <li>Duration: 10–18 months</li>
                <li>Needs irrigation</li>
                <li>High yield in black soil</li>
            </ul>

            <b>3️⃣ Soybean</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Season: Kharif</li>
                <li>Rainfall: 60–80 cm</li>
                <li>Temperature: 20–30°C</li>
                <li>Duration: 90–120 days</li>
            </ul>

            <b>4️⃣ Wheat</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Season: Rabi</li>
                <li>Rainfall: 50–75 cm</li>
                <li>Temperature: 10–25°C</li>
                <li>Duration: 120–150 days</li>
            </ul>

            <b>5️⃣ Jowar (Sorghum)</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Season: Kharif / Rabi</li>
                <li>Rainfall: 40–60 cm</li>
                <li>Temperature: 25–32°C</li>
                <li>Duration: 90–110 days</li>
            </ul>

            <b>6️⃣ Pulses (Chickpea, Pigeon pea)</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Rainfall: 40–60 cm</li>
                <li>Duration: 90–120 days</li>
                <li>Improve soil fertility</li>
            </ul>

            <b>7️⃣ Oilseeds (Sunflower, Linseed)</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Rainfall: 40–60 cm</li>
                <li>Duration: 80–120 days</li>
            </ul>

            <hr>

            <h2>📊 Summary Table</h2>

            <table>
                <tr>
                    <th>Feature</th>
                    <th>Black Soil</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Water holding</td>
                    <td>Very high</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Texture</td>
                    <td>Clayey</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Best crop</td>
                    <td>Cotton</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Fertility</td>
                    <td>Medium</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>pH</td>
                    <td>Slightly alkaline</td>
                </tr>
            </table>

            <h2>📝 Short Summary</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Black soil is also called Regur soil</li>
                <li>Best for cotton cultivation</li>
                <li>Holds moisture for a long time</li>
                <li>Cracks help in natural aeration</li>
                <li>Needs nitrogen & phosphorus fertilizers</li>
            </ul>

        </section>

    </div>

</div>

</body>
</html>
